Vowels.

The vowel count of a word (text) is a whole number:
the number of letters in the letters of the word in lower case where "aeiou" contains the letter.

A word (text) is all consonants when:
the vowel count of the word is 0.

For example, the vowel count of "Kite" is 2.
For example, the vowel count of "AEIOU" is 5.
For example, "rhythm" is all consonants.
For example, "kite" is not all consonants.
